From f7188e7415b1cb2e3c6e1af20a393411f6572a61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JuggyMcNutty <11588877+JuggyMcNutty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:46:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] BspClipper: the non-SSE build skips clipping for triangles
 inside the view

FORK ONLY. This project ships a NO-AI Code Rule asking that LLM-written
changes stay in a fork and are never PR'd upstream. These were written with
Claude. Do not submit them.

ClipEdge checks whether any of a triangle's clip distances is negative
and, when none is, returns the triangle as it is. The SSE path tests that
correctly; the plain C++ path, which every non-x86 build takes (Precomp.h
defines NOSSE there), tested clipd[i] -- a vertex index, and the value's
truth rather than its sign -- so the test was true for almost every
triangle, and on the handheld every visibility test went through the full
six-plane clipping loop: ClipEdge was the largest single function of the
visibility pass on the Cortex-A53 (~5 ms a frame on Liberty Island).

The test is now the SSE path's, with a NaN distance counted as needing
clipping. Whenever it lets a triangle skip, every distance is at least
zero, and the loop returns the triangle's own three vertices with weights
of exactly 1 and 0: the result is the same. A standalone test ran the old
and new test through that loop on a million random triangles (inside,
crossing the planes, degenerate, some with NaNs): 48% skipped, no
difference in vertices or weights.
---
 SurrealEngine/Render/BspClipper.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/SurrealEngine/Render/BspClipper.cpp b/SurrealEngine/Render/BspClipper.cpp
index 86b5052..ce340f3 100644
--- a/SurrealEngine/Render/BspClipper.cpp
+++ b/SurrealEngine/Render/BspClipper.cpp
@@ -432,8 +432,9 @@ int BspClipper::ClipEdge(const ShadedVertex* const* verts)
 		//clipd[6] = v.gl_ClipDistance[0];
 		//clipd[7] = v.gl_ClipDistance[1];
 		//clipd[8] = v.gl_ClipDistance[2];
+		// Any distance not at least zero (a NaN too) means clipping, as the SSE path tests
 		for (int j = 0; j < numclipdistances; j++)
-			needsclipping = needsclipping || clipd[i];
+			needsclipping = needsclipping || !(clipd[j] >= 0.0f);
 		clipd += numclipdistances;
 	}
 
